%% V02 Test Seq 03
%% Concrete DnD pending-choice: Paladin Divine Smite on confirmed hit.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor PaladinUI as Active Player UI
  participant Transport as WS/REST Handler
  participant Service as ActionExecutionApplicationService
  participant Graph as OperationGraphStage
  participant Choice as Choice Automation Policy
  participant RollPolicy as Manual Roll Policy
  participant Exec as OutcomeExecutionStage
  participant Events as Event Publisher

  Note over PaladinUI,Service: Encounter setup\nPaladinAlden Longsword attack modifier 7, damage 1d8 plus 4\nGhoul AC 12, HP 22\nChoice node divine_smite when predicate on_hit

  PaladinUI->>Transport: execute_action(req-2201, action.weapon_attack.longsword)
  Transport->>Service: execute_action(command)

  Service->>Graph: build and linearize graph
  Graph-->>Service: [op-2201-swing, op-2201-choice-divine-smite]
  Note over Service: Internal trace only: graph and per-operation stage lifecycle
  Service->>Exec: roll attack d20 11, total 18 vs AC 12 hit
  Service->>Exec: base damage node prepared for manual entry mode
  Exec-->>Service: predicate on_hit is true

  Service->>Choice: evaluate choice_ref divine_smite with valid slots 1 and 2

  alt Automation policy matches
    Choice-->>Service: choice_result slot_level 2
    Service->>Exec: inject smite rider and continue
    Service->>Exec: roll smite damage 3d8 values 5 7 2 total 14 radiant
    Exec-->>Service: total damage 24
  else Manual choice required
    Choice-->>Service: requires_player_choice
    Service-->>Transport: ActionExecutionOutcome with status pending_choice, choice_context, and target_operation_id
    Transport-->>PaladinUI: pending_choice prompt
    PaladinUI->>Transport: continue_action(req-2201, choice_result slot_level 2)
    Transport->>Service: resume_from_choice(req-2201)
    Service->>Exec: consume slot and apply rider
    Service->>Exec: smite rider node prepared for manual entry mode
  end

  Service->>RollPolicy: evaluate manual roll mode for weapon and smite damage nodes
  RollPolicy-->>Service: requires_pending_roll
  Service-->>Transport: ActionExecutionOutcome status pending_roll with roll_context weapon 1d8 plus 4 and smite 3d8
  Transport-->>PaladinUI: pending_roll prompt for combined damage entry
  PaladinUI->>Transport: continue_action req-2201 submitted_roll weapon_total 10 smite_total 14
  Transport->>Service: resume_from_roll req-2201
  Service->>Exec: validate submitted roll bounds and apply total damage 24
  Exec-->>Service: resumed total damage 24

  Service->>Events: attack_result hit on Ghoul
  Service->>Events: actor_damaged Ghoul amount 24 split slashing and radiant
  Service->>Events: turn_budget_updated
  Service->>Events: terminal_action_result resolved with request_id req-2201
  Events-->>PaladinUI: final deterministic batch

  Note over Service,Choice: Assertions\n1. Base damage is 10 and smite rider damage is 14 from submitted manual roll\n2. Final Ghoul HP delta is 24 damage and HP moves from 22 to 0\n3. Manual path emits one pending_choice and one pending_roll state\n4. Public stream focuses on gameplay outcomes, not stage lifecycle internals\n5. Automation and manual choice paths converge to same deterministic outcome after roll validation
